# No getty on any terminal: ttyS0 is the kernel console, ttyS1 belongs to the agent, and the
# display belongs to X. There is no ctrlaltdel entry either, so busybox init ignores the
# Ctrl+Alt+Del a student can type into the display instead of rebooting.
::sysinit:/sbin/openrc sysinit
::sysinit:/sbin/openrc boot
::wait:/sbin/openrc default
::shutdown:/sbin/openrc shutdown
# The agent, on the page's control line. init starts it again if it dies, and it opens with an
# unasked READY so the host knows it did.
::respawn:/usr/local/bin/icc-agent --serial /dev/ttyS1
